          "hidden": true
        }
      ],
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": 0,
          "show": [
            "dns",
            "a1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 1,
          "show": [
            "node",
            "a2",
            "traefik",
            "a3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 2,
          "show": [
            "svc",
            "a4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 3,
          "show": [
            "p1",
            "p2",
            "a5",
            "a6"
          ],
          "flow": [
            "a2",
            "a3",
            "a4",
            "a5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 4,
          "flow": [],
          "focus": [
            "svc",
            "traefik",
            "dns"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "First, the laptop asks the company's DNS server where go.corp.internal is, and gets back the addresses of our nodes."
        },
        {
          "text": "It connects to one of them on port 80, where ServiceLB is listening, and the request is handed to Traefik."
        },
        {
          "text": "Traefik checks its Ingress rules, finds our host name, and passes the request to the golinks Service."
        },
        {
          "text": "And the Service sends it to one of the ready pods."
        },
        {
          "text": "We'll build it from the inside out: the Service first, then the Ingress, then DNS.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "svc-yaml",
      "type": "code",
      "file": "manifests/base/golinks-service.yaml",
      "highlights": [
        {
          "at": 0,
          "lines": [
            1,
            8
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 1,
          "lines": [
            9,
            9
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 2,
          "lines": [
            10,
            11
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 3,
          "lines": [
            12,
            15
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "A Service gives a changing set of pods one stable address and one name."
        },
        {
          "text": "This one is type ClusterIP: an address that only works inside the cluster."
        },
        {
          "text": "Its selector is the label our pods carry, so any pod with that label can get its traffic."
        },
        {
          "text": "It listens on port 80, and forwards to the port named http on each pod, which is 8080.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.3
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "svc-apply",
      "type": "terminal",
      "title": "~/k8s-videos",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": 0,
          "command": "kubectl apply -f manifests/base/golinks-service.yaml",
          "output": [
            "service/golinks created"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 1,
          "command": "kubectl get svc golinks -n golinks",
          "output": [
            "NAME      TYPE        CLUSTER-IP     EXTERNAL-IP   PORT(S)   AGE",
            "golinks   ClusterIP   10.43.87.142   <none>        80/TCP    5s"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 2,
          "command": "kubectl get endpointslices -n golinks",
          "output": [
            "NAME             ADDRESSTYPE   PORTS   ENDPOINTS              AGE",
            "golinks-x7k2m    IPv4          8080    10.42.1.15,10.42.2.9   5s",
            "postgres-8hq4d   IPv4          5432    10.42.1.12             58m"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Apply it."
        },
        {
          "text": "It gets a cluster IP from the range k3s keeps for Services, and that address stays the same for as long as the Service exists."
        },
        {
          "text": "Behind it, an EndpointSlice lists the pod addresses it sends to right now: our two API pods, on port 8080."
        },
        {
          "text": "Only ready pods make that list. That's what readiness really controls, and it's the heart of Episode 6."
        },
        {
          "text": "Inside the cluster, CoreDNS already answers golinks.golinks.svc.cluster.local with the Service's address. Outside, nothing does yet.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "servicelb",
      "type": "diagram",
      "title": "ServiceLB, the built-in load balancer",
      "boxes": [
        {
          "id": "tsvc",
          "label": "Service traefik",
          "sublabel": "type: LoadBalancer",
          "x": 600,
          "y": 40,
          "w": 400,
