          "kind": "group",
          "label": "k3s-server-1  10.0.0.11",
          "x": 60,
          "y": 260,
          "w": 460,
          "h": 460
        },
        {
          "id": "n2",
          "kind": "group",
          "label": "k3s-agent-1  10.0.0.21",
          "x": 570,
          "y": 260,
          "w": 460,
          "h": 460
        },
        {
          "id": "n3",
          "kind": "group",
          "label": "k3s-agent-2  10.0.0.22",
          "x": 1080,
          "y": 260,
          "w": 460,
          "h": 460
        },
        {
          "id": "lb1",
          "kind": "pod",
          "label": "svclb",
          "sublabel": "ports 80 and 443",
          "x": 110,
          "y": 360,
          "w": 360,
          "h": 100,
          "hidden": true
        },
        {
          "id": "lb2",
          "kind": "pod",
          "label": "svclb",
          "sublabel": "ports 80 and 443",
          "x": 620,
          "y": 360,
          "w": 360,
          "h": 100,
          "hidden": true
        },
        {
          "id": "lb3",
          "kind": "pod",
          "label": "svclb",
          "sublabel": "ports 80 and 443",
          "x": 1130,
          "y": 360,
          "w": 360,
          "h": 100,
          "hidden": true
        },
        {
          "id": "tr",
          "kind": "pod",
          "label": "traefik",
          "x": 620,
          "y": 580,
          "w": 360,
          "h": 90
        }
      ],
      "arrows": [
        {
          "id": "b1",
          "from": "lb1",
          "to": "tr",
          "hidden": true
        },
        {
          "id": "b2",
          "from": "lb2",
          "to": "tr",
          "hidden": true
        },
        {
          "id": "b3",
          "from": "lb3",
          "to": "tr",
          "hidden": true
        }
      ],
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": 0,
          "focus": [
            "tsvc",
            "tr"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 1,
          "focus": []
        },
        {
          "at": 2,
          "show": [
            "lb1",
            "lb2",
            "lb3",
            "b1",
            "b2",
            "b3"
          ],
          "flow": [
            "b1",
            "b2",
            "b3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 3,
          "flow": [],
          "tone": {
            "n1": "good",
            "n2": "good",
            "n3": "good"
          }
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Traefik already runs in kube-system, and it has a Service of its own, of type LoadBalancer."
        },
        {
          "text": "In a cloud, that type asks the provider for a load balancer. On-prem there's no provider, so k3s brings its own: ServiceLB."
        },
        {
          "text": "ServiceLB runs a small pod on every node that holds ports 80 and 443 open, and forwards whatever arrives to Traefik."
        },
        {
          "text": "So each node's own IP address is a way in, and those addresses become the load balancer's addresses.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lb-check",
      "type": "terminal",
      "title": "~/k8s-videos",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": 0,
          "command": "kubectl get pods -n kube-system | grep svclb",
          "output": [
            "svclb-traefik-2b4e1c7a-6hx2r              2/2     Running     0          12d",
            "svclb-traefik-2b4e1c7a-qw8lm              2/2     Running     0          12d",
            "svclb-traefik-2b4e1c7a-zk5vn              2/2     Running     0          12d"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 1,
          "command": "kubectl get svc traefik -n kube-system -o jsonpath='{..ip}'",
          "output": [
            "10.0.0.11 10.0.0.21 10.0.0.22"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Here are those pods, one per node, each with a container for port 80 and one for 443."
        },
        {
          "text": "And these are the addresses ServiceLB gave Traefik's Service: one per node.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ingress-yaml",
      "type": "code",
      "file": "manifests/base/golinks-ingress.yaml",
      "highlights": [
        {
          "at": 0,
          "lines": [
            2,
            8
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 1,
          "lines": [
            10,
            10
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 2,
          "lines": [
            12,
            12
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 3,
          "lines": [
            13,
            21
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 4,
          "lines": [
            1,
            1
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Next, the Ingress: a set of routing rules for Traefik."
        },
        {
          "text": "ingressClassName says which controller the rules are for: traefik, the one k3s ships."
        },
        {
          "text": "The rule matches requests for the host go.corp.internal."
        },
        {
          "text": "And every path under it goes to the golinks Service, on its port named http."
        },
        {
          "text": "It's plain HTTP for now. Episode 8 adds TLS.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.3
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ingress-apply",
      "type": "terminal",
      "title": "~/k8s-videos",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": 0,
          "command": "kubectl apply -f manifests/base/golinks-ingress.yaml",
          "output": [
            "ingress.networking.k8s.io/golinks created"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 1,
          "command": "kubectl describe ingress golinks -n golinks | grep -A4 Rules",
          "output": [
            "Rules:",
            "  Host              Path  Backends",
            "  ----              ----  --------",
            "  go.corp.internal",
            "                    /   golinks:http (10.42.1.15:8080,10.42.2.9:8080)"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Apply it."
        },
        {
          "text": "Traefik picks it up straight away: requests for go.corp.internal, on any path, go to the golinks Service, which right now means these two pods.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ingress-curl",
      "type": "terminal",
      "title": "~/k8s-videos",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": 0,
          "command": "curl -i http://10.0.0.11/standup",
          "output": [
            "HTTP/1.1 404 Not Found",
            "Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8",
            "X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff",
            "Date: Mon, 02 Nov 2026 14:42:07 GMT",
            "Content-Length: 19",
            "",
            "404 page not found"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 2,
          "command": "curl -i -H 'Host: go.corp.internal' http://10.0.0.11/standup",
          "output": [
            "HTTP/1.1 404 Not Found",
            "Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8",
            "Date: Mon, 02 Nov 2026 14:42:19 GMT",
            "Content-Length: 41",
            "",
            "<p>No link named <b>standup</b> yet.</p>"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Now try it, straight at one node's IP address."
        },
        {
          "text": "A 404, but look closely: plain text, page not found. That's Traefik saying no rule matched, because we didn't ask for go.corp.internal."
        },
        {
          "text": "Send the same request with the right Host header,"
        },
        {
          "text": "and it's a different 404: HTML, from our app. The request went all the way to a pod."
        },
        {
          "text": "There's no standup link yet, because creating links needs sign-in, and that comes in Episode 9.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "dns-server",
      "type": "terminal",
      "title": "admin@ns1",
      "prompt": "$",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": 1,
          "command": "grep '^go ' /etc/bind/db.corp.internal",
          "output": [
            "go      IN  A   10.0.0.11",
            "go      IN  A   10.0.0.21",
            "go      IN  A   10.0.0.22"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "The last hop is DNS, and it isn't Kubernetes at all. It's the company's own DNS server, the one that answers for corp.internal."
        },
        {
          "text": "On it, the name go gets three address records, one for each node.",
          "senses": {
            "records": "noun"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Whoever runs that server adds them, just like any other internal name.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.3
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "laptop",
      "type": "terminal",
      "title": "laptop",
      "prompt": "$",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": 0,
          "command": "dig +short go.corp.internal",
          "output": [
            "10.0.0.11",
            "10.0.0.21",
            "10.0.0.22"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 1,
          "command": "curl -i http://go.corp.internal/standup",
          "output": [
            "HTTP/1.1 404 Not Found",
            "Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8",
            "Date: Mon, 02 Nov 2026 14:42:19 GMT",
            "Content-Length: 41",
            "",
            "<p>No link named <b>standup</b> yet.</p>"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "From a laptop, the name now resolves to the three nodes."
        },
        {
          "text": "And the plain request works, with no tricks: go.corp.internal, all the way through to our app."
        },
        {
          "text": "That's the whole path, end to end.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
