      ],
      "arrows": [],
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": 1,
          "show": [
            "core",
            "c1",
            "c2",
            "cpods"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 2,
          "show": [
            "corp",
            "k1",
            "kpeople"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "One thing to keep straight: there are now two DNS systems."
        },
        {
          "text": "CoreDNS runs inside the cluster and answers cluster names, like postgres-0.postgres. Only pods ask it."
        },
        {
          "text": "The company DNS answers the names people type, like go.corp.internal. It knows nothing about pods, only the nodes.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.5
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "next",
      "type": "title",
      "kicker": "Coming up",
      "title": "Episode 6: Health checks",
      "subtitle": "Startup, liveness and readiness probes",
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "That's the way in: DNS to the nodes, ServiceLB to Traefik, an Ingress rule to the Service, and the Service to a ready pod."
        },
        {
          "text": "Next time, we look hard at that word ready, and at the probes that decide it.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.6
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
